	(text
		"DESIGN NOTES\nInput 9-36 V (12 V nominal, survives 24 V jump start, -33 V reverse, ISO 7637-2 pulses via D1).\nF1 + D1 at the connector, then LM74700-Q1 ideal diode (Q1): <15 mV drop, blocks reverse battery.\nFB1 + C4/C5 pi filter keeps buck ripple off the harness (CISPR 25).\nLM5164-Q1 100 V COT buck: 5.0 V / 1 A, 10 uA IQ (key for parked-vehicle battery drain).\nLayout: buck loop (C4-U2-L1-C8) <10 mm, SW node small, far from GNSS (see PCB notes)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 162.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7f959a43-2f84-505b-9eb3-0b265cd09fc1")
	)
	(text
		"PART NOTES (VERIFY = check against vendor datasheet before release)\nJ1: 1 +12V(BAT) 2 IGN 3 PANIC(SOS, to GND) 4 DIN1 5 GND 6 AIN1 7 DOUT1(relay low side) 8 GND\nF1: VERIFY MPN suffix\nU1: EN tied to ANODE (always on)\nC1: VCAP to ANODE\nFB1: VERIFY MPN / AEC-Q200 variant\nR1: UVLO start ~6.0 V with R2 (EN 1.5 V), 10 uA VERIFY\nR3: RON sets COT fsw ~300 kHz - VERIFY with LM5164 eq.\nR4: VOUT = 1.2 V x (1 + R4/R5) = 5.0 V\nR8: VIN 0-50 V -> 0-3.2 V (ADC1_CH0), 12 uA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 219.71 162.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2495f32b-7c7e-5566-be96-11c38cc718af")
	)
)
